  "problem": "Given that the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-{e}^{x}$  has a root in the interval $[1,2],$ use the Newton-Raphson process starting from ${x}_{0}=1$ to estimate the root. Round your final answer to three decimal places.\n\n$x\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the Newton-Raphson method is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{f({x}_{n})}{{f}^{\u2032}({x}_{n})}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{\u2032}({x}_{n})$ is the derivative of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)=(2{x}^{3}-{e}^{x})^{\u2032}=6{x}^{2}-{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{2{x}_{n}^{3}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}}{6{x}_{n}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{n}(6{x}_{n}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{n}})-(2{x}_{n}^{3}-{e}^{{x}_{n}})}{6{x}_{n}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}_{n}^{3}-{x}_{n}{e}^{{x}_{n}}+{e}^{{x}_{n}}}{6{x}_{n}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{n}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{4{x}_{0}^{3}-{x}_{0}{e}^{{x}_{0}}+{e}^{{x}_{0}}}{6{x}_{0}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{0}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1)^{3}-(1){e}^{1}+{e}^{1}}{6(1)^{2}-{e}^{1}} \\\\  & =1.218\\,873\u2026.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{4{x}_{1}^{3}-{x}_{1}{e}^{{x}_{1}}+{e}^{{x}_{1}}}{6{x}_{1}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{1}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1.218\\,873\u2026)^{3}-(1.218\\,873\u2026){e}^{1.218\\,873\u2026}+{e}^{1.218\\,873\u2026}}{6(1.218\\,873\u2026)^{2}-{e}^{1.218\\,873\u2026}} \\\\  & =1.175\\,790\u2026, \\\\ {x}_{3} & =\\frac{4{x}_{2}^{3}-{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{2}}+{e}^{{x}_{2}}}{6{x}_{2}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1.175\\,790\u2026)^{3}-(1.175\\,790\u2026){e}^{1.175\\,790\u2026}+{e}^{1.175\\,790\u2026}}{6(1.175\\,790\u2026)^{2}-{e}^{1.175\\,790\u2026}} \\\\  & =1.173\\,749\u2026, \\\\ {x}_{4} & =\\frac{4{x}_{3}^{3}-{x}_{2}{e}^{{x}_{3}}+{e}^{{x}_{3}}}{6{x}_{3}^{2}-{e}^{{x}_{3}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1.173\\,749\u2026)^{3}-(1.173\\,749\u2026){e}^{1.173\\,749\u2026}+{e}^{1.173\\,749\u2026}}{6(1.173\\,749\u2026)^{2}-{e}^{1.173\\,749\u2026}} \\\\  & =1.173\\,744\u2026,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the last two approximations ${x}_{3}\u22481.174$ and ${x}_{4}\u22481.174$ are the same when rounded to three decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the root of the function is $x\u22481.174,$ rounded to three decimal places.",
